  <section>
    <h2>Why the official route stops most people</h2>
    <p>Telegram does have a real cash-out system, but it was designed for monetisation, not for individuals unloading a balance. Four conditions have to be met at once:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>You must have earned the Stars</strong> — through paid posts, paid reactions, tips, or sales inside your bot or Mini App. Stars you purchased do not qualify.</li>
      <li><strong>You need a Fragment account</strong>, which means connecting a TON wallet.</li>
      <li><strong>You wait 21 days.</strong> Telegram holds earned Stars for a fixed period before they can be converted.</li>
      <li><strong>You still end up holding TON</strong>, not money. To get som you then need a crypto exchange, usually with KYC on a foreign platform.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>For someone in Uzbekistan, the last step is the real wall. Buying and selling TON from an Uzbek bank card is awkward, the rate moves several percent in a day, and exchange fees eat into whatever you were trying to recover.</p>
  </section>

